    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "ONU UHD SEVAV\nPOSTAG\nNEW YORK-ATLANTA ROUTE\nAIR MAIL SERVICE\nFIRST-FLICHT\nATLANTA, GA.\nKLANT\nP MAY 1\n6, PM\n1928\nGA:\nVIA AIR MAIL\nW. H. Wolfgang\n2274 witney Are\n→ Toledo\nOhio",
      "19N9/75. 010/B5\nGK\nADDRESS\nYOUR MAIL\nOL\nSTREET AND\nг.\n8261\nNV02012\nEW\n2002.011.0460",
      "CONTRACT AIR MAIL ROUL\nNBR. 19\n1951/2351\nNEW YORK - ATLANTA\nMAY 1 and 2 1928\nPITCAIRN AVIATION Inc\n(New York, Phildelphia, Washington, Richmond, Winston-Salem,\nGreensboro, High Point, Spartanburg, Atlanta)\nPilots: A.M. Banks, Eugene R. Brown, John S. Kytle, R.S. Malloy,\nJ. Morrissey, Verne E. Treat\nThe plane piloted by Verne Treat out of New York nosed over landing\nat Philadelphia.\n296 pounds of mail carried out of New York on the first flight.\nThis cover continued on from Atlanta on the first air mail plane\nAtlanta/New Orleans (CAM 23) •"
    ],
